    <string name="perm_music_title">Allow access to your music?</string>
    <string name="perm_music_body">Music Player needs to read the audio files on this device to show your songs, folders and albums. Your music is never uploaded.</string>
    <string name="perm_music_body_33">Music Player needs to read the audio files on this device to show your songs, folders and albums. Your music is never uploaded. Android will also ask to show the playback controls in the notification area.</string>
    <string name="perm_music_off_title">Music access is off</string>
    <string name="perm_music_off_body">Android will not ask again. Open this app\'s settings, choose Permissions, and allow access to music and audio.</string>
    <string name="perm_write_title">Allow deleting songs?</string>
    <string name="perm_write_body">On this version of Android the app needs your permission once to delete files from your device.</string>
    <string name="perm_write_settings">Android will not ask again. Open this app\'s settings, choose Permissions, and allow access to files and media.</string>
    <string name="perm_install_title">Allow installing updates?</string>
    <string name="perm_install_body">Android asks you once to let Music Player install apps. The app only installs files that come from this project\'s releases and carry its signature.</string>
    <string name="perm_bars_title">Make the bars follow the music?</string>
    <string name="perm_bars_body">To draw bars that move with your music, Android asks for microphone access. Music Player never uses the microphone: it only looks at the sound of its own music, and nothing is recorded or sent anywhere. If you say Not allowed, the bars still move, they just do not follow the sound. You can change this in Settings.</string>
    <string name="perm_bars_settings">Android will not ask again. Open this app\'s settings, choose Permissions, and allow the microphone.</string>
    <string name="perm_wallpaper_title">Use your wallpaper?</string>
    <string name="perm_wallpaper_body">Music Player asks Android for your wallpaper picture. It stays on this device. If Android refuses, the wallpaper\'s colours are used instead.</string>
